  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The current best (config_037, acc=0.706) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, but scgpt has never been tested in any experiment. The progression from pca→scvi yielded a meaningful +0.039 gain (config_019→config_031), and the image encoder upgrade (resnet50→ViT-L) added another +0.028 (config_031→config_037). The RNA encoder is the single most impactful design axis, and we have only tested 2 of 3 options. Config_049 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap from config_037, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder in the best overall setting. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new optimization direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and can focus remaining budget on finer-tuning (e.g., aggregation or fusion). This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty in the design space with a direct A/B comparison against the current best."
}

